  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance for Economic Crimes - Burma</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhance the operational effectiveness of the Myanmar Financial Intelligence Unit (MFIU) to include (a) issuance of guidance to improve the timeliness and quality of suspicious activity reporting; (b) strategic analysis of suspicious transaction reports; (c) development of standard operating procedures (SOPs) for data reception, processing, dissemination, feedback and information exchange; and (d) development of a MFIU operations manual; (e) statistical reporting as required by the Financial Action Task Force (FATF) Recommendations; and (f) support development of the electronic reporting system (ERS) and development of an analytic system. The project continues to focus on promoting the Central Bank of Myanmar (CBM), Ministry of Planning and Finance (MPF), Securities and Exchange Commission of Myanmar (SECM), and the MFIU supervisory capacity of financial institutions and designated non-financial businesses and professions (DNFBPs) respectively, consistent with risk-based principles of the work plan. The project also focuses on money laundering case development and asset forfeiture procedures support for law enforcement agencies.</narrative>
  </description>
